{"name":"Camille Pink","hex":"#eeb5b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"}],"entries":[{"title":"Camille (French singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Camille Dalmais, better known by her mononym Camille, is a French singer-songwriter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Camille_Dalmais_in_2024.jpg/330px-Camille_Dalmais_in_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camille_(French_singer)","wikidata":"Q242914"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Camille_20090121_Melbourne_1.jpg/500px-Camille_20090121_Melbourne_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Camille_20090121_Melbourne_1.jpg/500px-Camille_20090121_Melbourne_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Camille performing in 2009","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACamille_20090121_Melbourne_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.w